<title>UK: Semple Cochrane shares set debut premium.</title>
<headline>Semple Cochrane shares set debut premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Semple Cochrane Plc, the Scottish-based engineering services company, set a premium on their first day trading on the London Stock Exchange on Monday.</p>
<p>By 0925 GMT the shares were quoted at 216-1/2p in moderate trade of 562,564 shares. They were sold to institutional investors at 180p in a placing raising 4.5 million stg and valuing the company at 14.0 million stg.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the float, sponsored by Williams de Broe, will be used to increase Semple's working capital.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, +44 171 542 7945</p>
</text>
